    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43474" body-key="m1">
                        
                            alphabetical letter
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">م</span></b> 
                        
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَ</span> for the interrogative <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا</span> immediately following
a prep.: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا</span> in the S, K; and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِلَى</span> last
sentence. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِ</span> for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِنْ</span>: see an ex., from a poet,
voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُبَّ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُ ٱللّٰهِ</span> &amp;c.: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيْمُنُ اللّٰهِ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مّ</span> for
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُمّ</span>: see the latter.

